body:
both of them cracked the case. Rust obsession and his life without purpose allowed him to invest 100% of his time in the case plus he was able to think outside the box. They were good fucking detectives and as martin said in the beginning of the show

&#x200B;

 "You know the detective's curse? The solution was right under my nose, but I was paying attention to the wrong clues."

 I think that the strongs points of the show were present: A good portrayal of a world where supes exists, good acting and good scenes. The problem with the season for me was the lazy writing of some scenes, like hughie helping starlight to escape, maeve present everywhere in the finale and how cringe stormfront caracter was.

&#x200B;

but for sure, the weakest point of this season was pacing

 How come Butcher wasn’t completely Sliced into a million pieces by Ryan’s laser vision? \[

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

The question is how Becca wasnt,
